A||||13||Jeff Blowers||Code 32 - EGR||||5||
Z||000000||Jeff Blowers||11-01-2001||06:23 PM||||Recently my check engine light came on.  After I shut the car off it did not reappear when started again.  I read the code and got code 32 - EGR.  I have read that this could also be a vacuum leak, or possibly something other than a replacement of the EGR valve itself.  Any thoughts on what I might look at first?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-01-2001||08:52 PM||||Vacuum leak, all those old black rubber tubes, EGR valve, EGR solinoid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||11-01-2001||09:52 PM||||Larry is right, it is in that system. If the light comes on once you are up at highway speed, it more than likely is the solenoid. Turn the engine off, restart and there is no light, get up to highway speed for a few miles, light comes on = solenoid.<P>You can check the EGR valve this way - unplug the small vacuum line from the valve, put your finger up under and into the diaphragm of the EGR valve and push up. While holding up the diaphragm, place your finger over the inlet. Then let go of the diaphragm and then remove your finger from the inlet - you should hear/feel the diaphragm drop down......<P>If it is a vacuum leak, more often than not your engine rpm's will be higher than normal.<P>Otherwise, it is the solenoid......<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A><p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||grinthock||11-01-2001||10:00 PM||||Had the same problem on my 85GT, there was instructions somewhere on the net on how to Backwash the solonoid||||reg||1
Z||000004||DR650SE||11-01-2001||10:07 PM||||I get a code 32 on the highway because I have a super high flow exhaust.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||6
Z||000005||G-Nasty||11-02-2001||03:16 AM||||Just got the same code 3 flashes pause 2 more-must be contagious. I did soul searching and will replace both the EGR & EGR soleniod- You should to. Just hope they dont set me back 2 many duckies.||||reg||1
Z||000006||SLYGUY||11-02-2001||03:22 AM||||The EGR system can be a real PITA. That was the one and only code I came across when I bought my car. Changed the EGR and it is okay now. <P>GRRRR!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.freakygamers.com/smilies/s/contrib/edoom/heads_or_tails.gif"> <P>Sly<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||ICAL||11-02-2001||03:56 PM||||I had the same problem with my 2.8L setting code 32 only after driving at highway speeds. The solution was to purchase the EGR solenoid, part number 10038324 from gmpartsdirect.com for $66 USD. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||11-02-2001||04:26 PM||||Is $66 standard for the EGR?  I too ocassionally get Code 32 (did again last night even).||||reg||1
